WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.629 --> 00:00:02.508
- What's up everybody?

00:00:02.508 --> 00:00:03.852
Welcome to another YouTube Hangout.

00:00:03.852 --> 00:00:05.133
Super excited to be here.

00:00:05.133 --> 00:00:09.656
I have a special guest with
me, Mr Dan Pena known as

00:00:09.656 --> 00:00:11.888
the $50 billion man.

00:00:11.888 --> 00:00:14.789
Because the people who he
has coached have went on

00:00:14.789 --> 00:00:17.938
to create $50 billion plus
in wealth for themselves

00:00:17.938 --> 00:00:18.899
and the world.

00:00:18.899 --> 00:00:21.558
He is a coach, he is an
author, he is a speaker,

00:00:21.558 --> 00:00:23.525
he's got a speaking tour right now.

00:00:23.525 --> 00:00:25.585
He's sometimes controversial, so we'll see

00:00:25.585 --> 00:00:30.190
what we get into today, Mr
Dan Pena, welcome aboard!

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:31.964
- Thank you for having me.

00:00:31.964 --> 00:00:34.413
It's nice to see your face

00:00:34.413 --> 00:00:38.731
other than on a website,
more or less in person.

00:00:38.731 --> 00:00:40.335
Thank you very much for having me.

00:00:40.335 --> 00:00:42.481
- I love it, so for the
people who may not have

00:00:42.481 --> 00:00:44.479
heard of you yet, we've
done some videos on you,

00:00:44.479 --> 00:00:46.558
but for the people who still
don't know, Mr Dan Pena,

00:00:46.558 --> 00:00:48.793
a little bit beyond the intro I gave you,

00:00:48.793 --> 00:00:50.600
how would you introduce yourself?

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:52.536
What do you want to say?

00:00:52.536 --> 00:00:53.703
- Well, I'm a,

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:57.815
barrio bad boy, I came from the

00:00:57.815 --> 00:01:00.851
barrio of East Los
Angeles, as a adolescent,

00:01:00.851 --> 00:01:03.208
got in a lot of trouble.

00:01:03.208 --> 00:01:05.441
Who got flunked out of
university three times,

00:01:05.441 --> 00:01:07.165
arrested five times,

00:01:07.165 --> 00:01:09.752
went off and the military
made a man of me, in fact,

00:01:09.752 --> 00:01:12.624
today is a very special day.

00:01:12.624 --> 00:01:15.541
50 years ago today, one June, 1967,

00:01:18.391 --> 00:01:21.270
by an act of congress, of
the United States of America,

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:23.542
I was deemed an officer and a gentleman,

00:01:23.542 --> 00:01:25.209
a second lieutenant.

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:27.855
- All right.
- So 50 that was

00:01:27.855 --> 00:01:28.837
(audio muting) high performance thing

00:01:28.837 --> 00:01:30.903
that I ever achieved 'cause I didn't think

00:01:30.903 --> 00:01:32.476
flunking out of school
and getting arrested

00:01:32.476 --> 00:01:34.143
was much of an achievement, although my

00:01:34.143 --> 00:01:36.393
buddies thought I was cool.

00:01:37.589 --> 00:01:40.846
And that's why I tell
kids, show me your friends

00:01:40.846 --> 00:01:42.415
and I'll show you your future.

00:01:42.415 --> 00:01:44.382
I went on, came back from the military,

00:01:44.382 --> 00:01:47.400
came back to school,
graduated with honors,

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:49.744
ultimately finished four year degree

00:01:49.744 --> 00:01:52.793
in two and a half years, went on,

00:01:52.793 --> 00:01:55.350
had a scholarship to go to
law school I never used,

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:57.869
and went on to Wall Street,

00:01:57.869 --> 00:01:59.814
and the rest is more or less history.

00:01:59.814 --> 00:02:00.647
And

00:02:01.534 --> 00:02:05.701
I've created since 1993, my
24th anniversary was last week,

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:09.668
when I gave my first seminar.

00:02:09.668 --> 00:02:13.835
And my kids, like you have
created over $50 billion in

00:02:14.746 --> 00:02:18.492
equity and value in those 24 years.

00:02:18.492 --> 00:02:20.512
And I was just on the
phone with one of them

00:02:20.512 --> 00:02:25.207
who's created billions and
he wishes you all well,

00:02:25.207 --> 00:02:27.685
and he says, you'll
need it under the whip!

00:02:27.685 --> 00:02:29.054
I'm the whip.

00:02:29.054 --> 00:02:30.695
- [Evan] I like it.

00:02:30.695 --> 00:02:31.612
- Yeah and,

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:36.011
I've just started a tour of
the United States and Canada,

00:02:36.011 --> 00:02:38.899
and I'll be visiting your
hometown in a few months,

00:02:38.899 --> 00:02:42.321
where I go to speak at
universities for free pro bono.

00:02:42.321 --> 00:02:43.652
They don't pay for me to get there

00:02:43.652 --> 00:02:45.664
or anything like that, they
don't put me up in a hotel.

00:02:45.664 --> 00:02:48.662
And I got the idea, Evan,
when Oxford University

00:02:48.662 --> 00:02:52.484
called me last year, and
I had speciously said,

00:02:52.484 --> 00:02:55.644
oh must be my Rhodes
Scholarship, 50 years late.

00:02:55.644 --> 00:02:56.937
You know?

00:02:56.937 --> 00:02:59.600
But I went to speak
there, and it was a very

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:01.094
successful event.

00:03:01.094 --> 00:03:04.660
And then I got the idea
well, if Oxford liked it,

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:06.590
maybe a lot of other people would like it.

00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:08.324
But I was booked up all
the rest of last year

00:03:08.324 --> 00:03:11.350
and so I only started giving
these talks to schools.

00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:14.530
But everything I have
on my website is free,

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:18.994
99.9% of all the kids that I've
created the $50 billion with

00:03:18.994 --> 00:03:22.729
I've never met because
all my product's free.

00:03:22.729 --> 00:03:25.881
I don't sell anything other
than the Castle Seminar,

00:03:25.881 --> 00:03:27.945
and then I mentor you for a year free.

00:03:27.945 --> 00:03:28.778
But,

00:03:30.517 --> 00:03:32.728
I mean the big thing about today is,

00:03:32.728 --> 00:03:34.354
information's almost instantaneous,

00:03:34.354 --> 00:03:35.744
actually it is instantaneous.

00:03:35.744 --> 00:03:39.194
Like this, you're in
Canada and I'm in Scotland,

00:03:39.194 --> 00:03:40.544
and we're able to do a show like this.

00:03:40.544 --> 00:03:42.097
And I think it's terrific.

00:03:42.097 --> 00:03:44.059
I take my hat off to you.

00:03:44.059 --> 00:03:45.868
- I love it, so let's get to the topic.

00:03:45.868 --> 00:03:48.093
I always have my guests pick the topic.

00:03:48.093 --> 00:03:50.905
I don't really cover politics
a lot on this channel.

00:03:50.905 --> 00:03:53.648
You know I always feel like entrepreneurs,

00:03:53.648 --> 00:03:55.160
we're the ones that's going
to solve all the problems

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:57.820
of the world, not to
rely on the president,

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:00.936
or the government, or not
to blame the president

00:04:00.936 --> 00:04:03.053
for your not having success.

00:04:03.053 --> 00:04:04.785
Right like, I'm not a
success because of Trump

00:04:04.785 --> 00:04:07.438
or because of Obama or
because of anybody else,

00:04:07.438 --> 00:04:09.395
I think is ridiculous.

00:04:09.395 --> 00:04:12.076
And so it's interesting to
cover politics on this channel,

00:04:12.076 --> 00:04:14.286
I'd love to know why you picked this topic

00:04:14.286 --> 00:04:16.368
and what your thoughts are.

00:04:16.368 --> 00:04:19.844
- Well, on November eighth, I announced,

00:04:19.844 --> 00:04:23.087
when he was elected, now, full disclosure,

00:04:23.087 --> 00:04:26.308
I knew President Trump
in a different life.

00:04:26.308 --> 00:04:28.614
I knew him in the late '80s and early '90s

00:04:28.614 --> 00:04:32.082
when I was partners with people
that he knew in New York.

00:04:32.082 --> 00:04:35.312
But I haven't seen
President Trump in 25 years.

00:04:35.312 --> 00:04:36.940
So OK.

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:38.738
But on November eighth,
I said that this was

00:04:38.738 --> 00:04:41.536
the greatest transformation
of wealth in the history

00:04:41.536 --> 00:04:44.278
of the world since World War II.

00:04:44.278 --> 00:04:47.091
And the reason why he was
elected in my judgment,

00:04:47.091 --> 00:04:50.456
and I was one of the first
to endorse him, publicly.

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:53.456
Is that the United States is fed up,

00:04:54.677 --> 00:04:57.438
you know, I'm not here
to talk bad about Obama,

00:04:57.438 --> 00:05:00.406
although I didn't think
he did much, but anyway,

00:05:00.406 --> 00:05:02.812
and just fed up, just
like Brexit in the UK,

00:05:02.812 --> 00:05:04.393
and various other votes.

00:05:04.393 --> 00:05:08.320
But I know what he's capable
of, both good and bad,

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:09.237
and I know,

00:05:10.667 --> 00:05:13.834
most people listening here,
if they're US citizens,

00:05:13.834 --> 00:05:15.905
have no idea what it
really means if we get

00:05:15.905 --> 00:05:19.810
from 35 to 50 or 20% corporate tax rate.

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:22.400
You have no conception what that means.

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:24.103
I mean in the trickle down effect.

00:05:24.103 --> 00:05:28.270
So I mean the Trump era, and
he may only stay one term,

00:05:29.755 --> 00:05:32.742
but the Trump era, he's already
made tremendous changes.

00:05:32.742 --> 00:05:36.395
And if he's done nothing more than

00:05:36.395 --> 00:05:40.271
we can have change if the people rise up.

00:05:40.271 --> 00:05:41.988
We can have change if the people rise up.

00:05:41.988 --> 00:05:44.608
Now, as another aside,

00:05:44.608 --> 00:05:46.608
I knew the first Trudeau

00:05:49.042 --> 00:05:52.231
back in the day, probably
before you were born.

00:05:52.231 --> 00:05:54.265
And I had the pleasure of meeting him.

00:05:54.265 --> 00:05:57.932
And just as I also have
met five presidents,

00:05:58.859 --> 00:06:03.026
five secretaries of state, and
I also met, as a little boy,

00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:06.803
General de Gaulle.

00:06:06.803 --> 00:06:11.084
So when you've been around a
million years, like I have,

00:06:11.084 --> 00:06:13.821
you've met a lot of people, and that's why

00:06:13.821 --> 00:06:16.228
the perspective that I give, and I believe

00:06:16.228 --> 00:06:18.334
why I was so successful at Oxford,

00:06:18.334 --> 00:06:20.691
and I'm going to be successful
at these other schools,

00:06:20.691 --> 00:06:22.318
and that's why the kids come here.

00:06:22.318 --> 00:06:25.880
My demographics for this
seminar, Evan has changed.

00:06:25.880 --> 00:06:29.213
10 years ago it was mid 30s to late 40s.

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:33.478
The demographics for the
seminar now is late teens

00:06:33.478 --> 00:06:34.949
to late 20s.

00:06:34.949 --> 00:06:36.513
- [Evan] Hmm.

00:06:36.513 --> 00:06:38.378
- Late teens to late 20s.

00:06:38.378 --> 00:06:40.497
- And why the shift?

00:06:40.497 --> 00:06:42.710
- Two things, I believe.

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:46.359
One the kids can make
money on the internet

00:06:46.359 --> 00:06:50.057
to pay for it, although we
give students a big discount

00:06:50.057 --> 00:06:52.912
and we give active duty
military a big discount,

00:06:52.912 --> 00:06:54.521
that's number one.

00:06:54.521 --> 00:06:57.366
And number two, they know
that they're pissed off

00:06:57.366 --> 00:07:00.783
earlier now, they know they're not happy.

00:07:01.763 --> 00:07:04.423
And people only make a change
for one or two reasons,

00:07:04.423 --> 00:07:07.414
you know, inspiration or desperation.

00:07:07.414 --> 00:07:10.029
And to come to me because I'm really hard,

00:07:10.029 --> 00:07:11.734
to come to me you have to have tried

00:07:11.734 --> 00:07:14.450
everybody and their dog.

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:18.533
I've had kids come here
that have read 700 books.

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:23.714
And in 700 books they couldn't
figure what the fuck to do.

00:07:23.714 --> 00:07:25.517
So they come to me.

00:07:25.517 --> 00:07:28.492
And the most important aspect
in my coaching, teaching,

00:07:28.492 --> 00:07:31.464
mentoring is the one
year free mentor program,

00:07:31.464 --> 00:07:33.831
and I give it free because
I want to be able to

00:07:33.831 --> 00:07:35.915
throw you out if you don't measure up.

00:07:35.915 --> 00:07:40.066
I take exception to people
that say it's a boot camp.

00:07:40.066 --> 00:07:43.629
Most of these kids have never
been to a fucking boot camp.

00:07:43.629 --> 00:07:48.018
They wouldn't know a boot camp
if it bit them in the butt!

00:07:48.018 --> 00:07:49.943
But I mean, we're hard here.

00:07:49.943 --> 00:07:54.454
Like the kids can't go to the
gymnasium until they earn it.

00:07:54.454 --> 00:07:57.871
I have two gymnasiums here at the castle.

00:08:00.345 --> 00:08:01.562
It's hard.

00:08:01.562 --> 00:08:04.183
But I find life hard and,

00:08:04.183 --> 00:08:07.270
if you look back upon the
Elon Musks, et cetera,

00:08:07.270 --> 00:08:09.979
of this world, the current
day, they're tough guys,

00:08:09.979 --> 00:08:12.290
they're not, you know, wusses.

00:08:12.290 --> 00:08:15.824
You know, they're not
snowflakes I think is the word.

00:08:15.824 --> 00:08:17.873
I had to look that up, I
wasn't sure what that meant.

00:08:17.873 --> 00:08:19.806
But they're not snowflakes.

00:08:19.806 --> 00:08:22.376
And most people come here, I'm told,

00:08:22.376 --> 00:08:26.284
because I'm an alpha male dad
model that they never had.

00:08:26.284 --> 00:08:28.889
I'm not asking for any kids,
I got three lovely children,

00:08:28.889 --> 00:08:30.264
I don't need any.

00:08:30.264 --> 00:08:33.301
But one of the reasons
that I have admiration

00:08:33.301 --> 00:08:36.187
for President Trump, look at his kids.

00:08:36.187 --> 00:08:37.402
They should be spoiled brats.

00:08:37.402 --> 00:08:39.162
Now I'm not saying they're
not spoiled in a certain way

00:08:39.162 --> 00:08:41.125
but they've got their
heads on their shoulder,

00:08:41.125 --> 00:08:43.041
they've got their own business.

00:08:43.041 --> 00:08:46.022
My kids should be spoiled brats.

00:08:46.022 --> 00:08:48.675
But they're not, they're
successful in their own,

00:08:48.675 --> 00:08:50.131
I didn't get any of my children jobs,

00:08:50.131 --> 00:08:51.829
I didn't make one phone call.

00:08:51.829 --> 00:08:53.859
And they went to good schools.

00:08:53.859 --> 00:08:55.371
You don't have to go to school.

00:08:55.371 --> 00:08:56.751
We have kids that come here

00:08:56.751 --> 00:08:58.301
that didn't get out of high school.

00:08:58.301 --> 00:09:01.932
The point is that I make you accountable.

00:09:01.932 --> 00:09:04.769
I'm the only, that I
know of, and correct me

00:09:04.769 --> 00:09:08.290
if you know of anybody else
that makes their seminar

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:11.723
attendees and post seminar, for one year,

00:09:11.723 --> 00:09:14.056
to be 100% accountable.

00:09:15.429 --> 00:09:16.884
100%.

00:09:16.884 --> 00:09:17.967
Not 98%.

00:09:19.315 --> 00:09:23.482
Through their weekly reporting
and their monthly Zoom calls.

00:09:25.886 --> 00:09:27.736
It's very much like the military.

00:09:27.736 --> 00:09:31.010
And, the only thing is
I don't hit 'em anymore.

00:09:31.010 --> 00:09:33.327
In the '90s, I hit ya.

00:09:33.327 --> 00:09:34.700
Now I don't.

00:09:34.700 --> 00:09:36.233
I'd still like to hit ya.

00:09:36.233 --> 00:09:38.436
But now for obvious reasons,
everybody's got an iPhone.

00:09:38.436 --> 00:09:40.751
Although, we don't let you
have your iPhones in the room,

00:09:40.751 --> 00:09:43.460
but anyway, be that as it may, right now,

00:09:43.460 --> 00:09:45.302
there's a whole room
full of them sitting over

00:09:45.302 --> 00:09:46.928
in the main castle waiting to come

00:09:46.928 --> 00:09:49.144
and me giving them a beatin'!

00:09:49.144 --> 00:09:50.549
Or a beat down.

00:09:50.549 --> 00:09:53.665
And we've even got some Canadians!

00:09:53.665 --> 00:09:56.979
The Canadians love me, I don't
know why, why they should.

00:09:56.979 --> 00:09:59.671
I normally don't have anything
good to say about Canada but,

00:09:59.671 --> 00:10:02.837
other than I made a lot of money there.

00:10:02.837 --> 00:10:04.986
And yourself, who's been kind enough to

00:10:04.986 --> 00:10:07.170
talk about me over the years.

00:10:07.170 --> 00:10:10.003
And like my 10 secrets, et cetera.

00:10:11.606 --> 00:10:13.760
I think it's a very unique
concept that you have.

00:10:13.760 --> 00:10:15.992
And I think you bring a
lot of service to the kids.

00:10:15.992 --> 00:10:19.021
But at the end of the day
they've got to take action.

00:10:19.021 --> 00:10:22.439
They can watch all the YouTubes, podcast,

00:10:22.439 --> 00:10:25.582
from now until they bury them.

00:10:25.582 --> 00:10:28.292
And if they don't take action it's all BS.

00:10:28.292 --> 00:10:30.320
The Dalai Lama had his
80th birthday last year.

00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:32.179
Were you invited, by the way?

00:10:32.179 --> 00:10:34.077
- I was not invited.

00:10:34.077 --> 00:10:35.410
- Neither was I.

00:10:36.296 --> 00:10:39.039
But some of my high performers were.

00:10:39.039 --> 00:10:43.867
And at the end of the speech
he says meditation is great.

00:10:43.867 --> 00:10:47.200
Prayer is great, contemplation is great.

00:10:48.148 --> 00:10:51.287
But if you don't take
action, action, action,

00:10:51.287 --> 00:10:53.204
all the rest is wasted.

00:10:55.003 --> 00:10:56.902
And what the kids today have trouble with,

00:10:56.902 --> 00:11:00.652
they connote reading a
book to taking action.

00:11:01.843 --> 00:11:03.435
And I'm not saying you shouldn't read

00:11:03.435 --> 00:11:05.157
'cause I've read the classics,
I've read Shakespeare,

00:11:05.157 --> 00:11:07.146
and all that stuff.

00:11:07.146 --> 00:11:09.132
But it's not taking action.

00:11:09.132 --> 00:11:11.150
Taking action is pulling the trigger,

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:12.925
going out and making something happen.

00:11:12.925 --> 00:11:14.645
And even if you fail.

00:11:14.645 --> 00:11:16.421
And the kids have problems with that.

00:11:16.421 --> 00:11:17.910
And they come to me

00:11:17.910 --> 00:11:22.013
and I show them the way
through the maze as it were,

00:11:22.013 --> 00:11:24.505
how to learn how to take action.

00:11:24.505 --> 00:11:25.555
- So let's talk about that.

00:11:25.555 --> 00:11:27.214
You've got the guys reading 700 books,

00:11:27.214 --> 00:11:29.035
you've got people just watching video

00:11:29.035 --> 00:11:30.976
after YouTube video after YouTube video,

00:11:30.976 --> 00:11:33.028
but they're not doing anything.

00:11:33.028 --> 00:11:35.663
They show up to you, how
do you get that person

00:11:35.663 --> 00:11:38.055
who read all the books but
hasn't pulled the trigger

00:11:38.055 --> 00:11:39.388
to do something?

00:11:40.327 --> 00:11:42.732
- Well first of all, they
pay me a whole bunch of money

00:11:42.732 --> 00:11:44.942
to come here, and there's no refunds.

00:11:44.942 --> 00:11:47.068
So they pay me a lot of money.

00:11:47.068 --> 00:11:48.372
And,

00:11:48.372 --> 00:11:49.455
I shame them.

00:11:50.950 --> 00:11:52.367
I embarrass them.

00:11:53.852 --> 00:11:57.358
Even yourself, high
performer, and by the way,

00:11:57.358 --> 00:11:59.241
I call everybody kids
because I'm either old enough

00:11:59.241 --> 00:12:00.864
to be your father or grandfather.

00:12:00.864 --> 00:12:03.649
A kid like you, if you had to keep track

00:12:03.649 --> 00:12:07.703
of seven days a week, 24
hours a day, what you do,

00:12:07.703 --> 00:12:12.117
you would be shocked,
astounded, overwhelmed,

00:12:12.117 --> 00:12:15.411
or as they say in Britain, gobsmacked,

00:12:15.411 --> 00:12:17.411
how much time you waste.

00:12:19.924 --> 00:12:24.091
And I make them keep track
of every minute of the day!

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:26.792
Every minute of the day.

00:12:26.792 --> 00:12:28.292
And it's not easy.

00:12:29.474 --> 00:12:31.112
It's not easy.

00:12:31.112 --> 00:12:33.029
And, when you find out,

00:12:34.397 --> 00:12:36.801
I have people that have
come to the seminar,

00:12:36.801 --> 00:12:38.884
that spend 20 hours a day

00:12:40.398 --> 00:12:43.687
walking in the fresh air and meditating.

00:12:43.687 --> 00:12:45.403
20 hours a week, excuse me, not a day.

00:12:45.403 --> 00:12:46.736
20 hours a week.

00:12:47.702 --> 00:12:50.141
And they don't get anything done,

00:12:50.141 --> 00:12:52.625
and they don't feel relaxed.

00:12:52.625 --> 00:12:56.983
Now I've never meditated
one second in my life.

00:12:56.983 --> 00:12:59.263
I've walked in the fresh air.

00:12:59.263 --> 00:13:01.358
But unless I'm sweating
and I'm running up a hill,

00:13:01.358 --> 00:13:04.441
I don't think I'm accomplishing much.

00:13:04.441 --> 00:13:06.848
From a cardio point of view.

00:13:06.848 --> 00:13:11.465
At my age, I should be
strolling, up the hill,

00:13:11.465 --> 00:13:13.582
or not even going up the hill.

00:13:13.582 --> 00:13:16.101
So we make 'em accountable,
we give 'em the templates,

00:13:16.101 --> 00:13:18.018
we give them the tools.

00:13:19.938 --> 00:13:21.886
For those that even didn't read 700 books,

00:13:21.886 --> 00:13:24.108
they've read seven books or 20 books,

00:13:24.108 --> 00:13:28.840
you've read about all the
various financial instruments.

00:13:28.840 --> 00:13:31.262
But here we teach you
how to play the entire

00:13:31.262 --> 00:13:34.603
financial orchestra for the first time.

00:13:34.603 --> 00:13:37.614
Money is almost free the
last eight or nine years.

00:13:37.614 --> 00:13:39.864
Yet it's hardly I find a snowflake

00:13:39.864 --> 00:13:42.063
that has done anything about it.

00:13:42.063 --> 00:13:44.146
Free, the money's free right now!

00:13:44.146 --> 00:13:48.313
10, 20 years from now,
Evan, the guys on this call,

00:13:48.313 --> 00:13:50.187
their kids and grandkids
are going to ask 'em,

00:13:50.187 --> 00:13:52.642
what the fuck did you do when the money

00:13:52.642 --> 00:13:54.213
was being given away free?

00:13:54.213 --> 00:13:55.380
Dad, granddad?

00:13:56.460 --> 00:13:59.086
I did nothing, I just
kept my finger up my ass,

00:13:59.086 --> 00:14:00.919
and read another book.

00:14:02.373 --> 00:14:03.206
I mean,

00:14:04.296 --> 00:14:07.756
I don't know how much longer this
is going to last, free money,

00:14:07.756 --> 00:14:11.364
but right now, there is
so much money out there,

00:14:11.364 --> 00:14:13.398
it's unbelievable.

00:14:13.398 --> 00:14:15.381
The problem the kids
have when they come here,

00:14:15.381 --> 00:14:17.668
and not just when they
come here, they don't know

00:14:17.668 --> 00:14:19.697
what a real deal looks like.

00:14:19.697 --> 00:14:22.858
They really don't know that
(sighing) free cash flow

00:14:22.858 --> 00:14:24.423
has to cover debt service.

00:14:24.423 --> 00:14:25.936
They don't understand that concept.

00:14:25.936 --> 00:14:28.498
And they come in here with PhDs, MBAs,

00:14:28.498 --> 00:14:30.454
they're certified financial
analysts, you name it

00:14:30.454 --> 00:14:31.882
we've had 'em here.

00:14:31.882 --> 00:14:33.300
And they just don't understand.

00:14:33.300 --> 00:14:34.773
As I said, they wouldn't know a deal

00:14:34.773 --> 00:14:36.577
if it bit 'em in the butt.

00:14:36.577 --> 00:14:39.556
And they spend most of their time on deals

00:14:39.556 --> 00:14:42.723
that intellectually sound good but,

00:14:42.723 --> 00:14:45.518
financially they're no good.

00:14:45.518 --> 00:14:49.263
And so once you learn
the difference between

00:14:49.263 --> 00:14:52.787
a deal and not a deal, and
once you learn for real,

00:14:52.787 --> 00:14:55.747
and we show you the templates to use

00:14:55.747 --> 00:14:58.467
to how to get the money out of the banks,

00:14:58.467 --> 00:15:03.074
your life is never the same,
it's just never the same.

00:15:03.074 --> 00:15:04.058
- And why now?

00:15:04.058 --> 00:15:05.772
So you say free money right
now, it's not going to last,

00:15:05.772 --> 00:15:08.946
next generation, what's
so special about right now

00:15:08.946 --> 00:15:10.639
where it's free money?
- Because interest rates

00:15:10.639 --> 00:15:11.972
are so damn low!

00:15:13.561 --> 00:15:17.092
I mean interest rates are giving it away!

00:15:17.092 --> 00:15:19.788
I mean, I was making money, millions,

00:15:19.788 --> 00:15:23.288
when interest rates were 15, 18, 20%!

00:15:24.643 --> 00:15:27.060
Not two, three, four percent.

00:15:29.181 --> 00:15:31.397
I mean they're literally, the
only thing they're not doing

00:15:31.397 --> 00:15:33.685
is setting up, like the
Bank of America founder,

00:15:33.685 --> 00:15:35.752
the picture you've got in the back,

00:15:35.752 --> 00:15:37.623
he said, if I remember correctly,

00:15:37.623 --> 00:15:41.052
after the great fire, San
Francisco Fire of 1906 or five

00:15:41.052 --> 00:15:43.768
or whatever it was, he set up a card table

00:15:43.768 --> 00:15:46.703
outside the bank, or what
was left of the bank,

00:15:46.703 --> 00:15:48.620
they were making loans.

00:15:50.468 --> 00:15:53.475
And people still didn't
even come up to him.

00:15:53.475 --> 00:15:57.629
He didn't even do all
the paperwork like now.

00:15:57.629 --> 00:15:58.879
I mean, oh God,

00:15:59.718 --> 00:16:03.801
I take a jet plane, I'd
be the number one in line

00:16:04.716 --> 00:16:07.170
to do business with that old timer.

00:16:07.170 --> 00:16:10.475
But I mean it's not that easy,
but I mean it's real easy.

00:16:10.475 --> 00:16:11.978
Another thing, in America,

00:16:11.978 --> 00:16:14.630
the Small Business Administration, the SBA

00:16:14.630 --> 00:16:17.321
in recent years has gone from
a one million dollar limit

00:16:17.321 --> 00:16:19.029
to a five million dollar limit.

00:16:19.029 --> 00:16:23.432
Meaning the government
guarantees your damn loan.

00:16:23.432 --> 00:16:25.734
And there's talk, under Trump,
I don't know if it's true,

00:16:25.734 --> 00:16:29.234
that it's going to go
to seven or 10 million.

00:16:30.461 --> 00:16:32.956
If you can't do a deal when
the government's going to

00:16:32.956 --> 00:16:34.853
guarantee 100% of the goddamn thing,

00:16:34.853 --> 00:16:37.520
you ought to blow your brains out!

00:16:39.295 --> 00:16:41.950
You ought to commit seppuku,
I think it's called.

00:16:41.950 --> 00:16:45.676
As Elon Musk said, he
would rather commit seppuku

00:16:45.676 --> 00:16:48.176
which is, harikari, than fail!

00:16:51.443 --> 00:16:52.360
And I mean,

00:16:54.269 --> 00:16:56.682
I don't know how long it's
going to last, I don't.

00:16:56.682 --> 00:17:00.073
But I do know that it's here now.

00:17:00.073 --> 00:17:02.535
And God almighty, I don't
know why you wouldn't

00:17:02.535 --> 00:17:03.660
want to take advantage of it.

00:17:03.660 --> 00:17:07.077
As long as it's moral, ethical and legal.

00:17:08.052 --> 00:17:10.676
Moral, ethical and legal.

00:17:10.676 --> 00:17:13.009
Those are my only backstops.

00:17:15.164 --> 00:17:16.988
- I like it.

00:17:16.988 --> 00:17:18.636
- But if you don't want to
be moral ethical and legal,

00:17:18.636 --> 00:17:19.719
God almighty.

00:17:21.059 --> 00:17:23.281
It'd be the mafia!

00:17:23.281 --> 00:17:24.784
- I like that you know your history!

00:17:24.784 --> 00:17:27.091
Most people have never
heard of AP Giannini,

00:17:27.091 --> 00:17:29.009
and being able to pull
that story out was great,

00:17:29.009 --> 00:17:32.150
it was actually across two
barrels and a plank of wood,

00:17:32.150 --> 00:17:34.575
and he would lend money to people

00:17:34.575 --> 00:17:37.649
based off of a handshake
and a look in their eye.

00:17:37.649 --> 00:17:39.615
That's how you got a
deal with AP Giannini.

00:17:39.615 --> 00:17:43.140
He wanted to judge a man by
the callouses on his hand,

00:17:43.140 --> 00:17:45.381
that's how he made a decision
whether to give a loan or not.

00:17:45.381 --> 00:17:47.074
So, far cry from
- All they have

00:17:47.074 --> 00:17:50.389
are callouses on their fingertips maybe

00:17:50.389 --> 00:17:52.273
from being on the laptop.

00:17:52.273 --> 00:17:54.393
(laughing)

00:17:54.393 --> 00:17:55.781
- Let's talk about that, so I mean,

00:17:55.781 --> 00:17:57.345
I got AP Giannini behind me.

00:17:57.345 --> 00:17:58.762
I love learning from successful people,

00:17:58.762 --> 00:18:00.495
trying to apply to my life, my business.

00:18:00.495 --> 00:18:03.408
I see behind you you've
got this giant wall

00:18:03.408 --> 00:18:06.355
called influencers, and on there you have

00:18:06.355 --> 00:18:08.408
some controversial figures, you've got,

00:18:08.408 --> 00:18:11.519
I saw Winston Churchill
and Jesus Christ and JFK.

00:18:11.519 --> 00:18:15.008
You have Adolf Hitler,
Einstein, Trump, Ted Turner,

00:18:15.008 --> 00:18:17.862
talk to me, you're
pulling from a wide range

00:18:17.862 --> 00:18:20.159
of people who are all over the place.

00:18:20.159 --> 00:18:23.159
- Stalin, I've got Stalin, I've got,

00:18:24.364 --> 00:18:27.281
oh Walt Disney, Jack Welch, I mean,

00:18:29.673 --> 00:18:34.125
McNamara from the Vietnam
era who I actually knew but

00:18:34.125 --> 00:18:36.109
all those people now, when they ask me,

00:18:36.109 --> 00:18:37.293
what have I read?

00:18:37.293 --> 00:18:38.293
I read them.

00:18:40.802 --> 00:18:44.969
What did I look at last night
to get fired up for today,

00:18:46.364 --> 00:18:47.364
for tonight?

00:18:49.812 --> 00:18:53.979
I watched the two and a half
hour movie, 1963 movie Zulu,

00:18:55.611 --> 00:18:57.194
with Michael Caine,

00:18:59.161 --> 00:19:01.661
which depicted 1779 I believe,

00:19:03.982 --> 00:19:07.899
Africa, the British army,
where they fought off

00:19:09.363 --> 00:19:11.113
5000 Zulus, 150 guys,

00:19:12.718 --> 00:19:14.885
and they did heroic stuff.

00:19:15.905 --> 00:19:18.321
That's what fires me up because it's tough

00:19:18.321 --> 00:19:20.773
to keep your energy high and fired up

00:19:20.773 --> 00:19:23.615
because I've done just about
everything known to man,

00:19:23.615 --> 00:19:24.729
I have.

00:19:24.729 --> 00:19:26.779
Not all good shit, but I mean, I've done

00:19:26.779 --> 00:19:28.753
just about everything known to man.

00:19:28.753 --> 00:19:30.898
But the reason I have these
people is because I learn

00:19:30.898 --> 00:19:32.996
something from everybody.

00:19:32.996 --> 00:19:37.996
You know, Hitler believed in
practice, practice, practice.

00:19:37.996 --> 00:19:41.672
He had over a million photographs of him

00:19:41.672 --> 00:19:45.485
to do his promotional
stuff when he was selling

00:19:45.485 --> 00:19:47.719
Mein Kampf, and when he was selling

00:19:47.719 --> 00:19:50.689
to become chancellor
of Germany in the '30s.

00:19:50.689 --> 00:19:52.210
A million pictures.

00:19:52.210 --> 00:19:56.172
He was the first guy
being advised by Goebbels

00:19:56.172 --> 00:19:59.346
that, you know, if you're
going to influence the masses.

00:19:59.346 --> 00:20:02.604
I studied when I was learning,
when I was a poor speaker

00:20:02.604 --> 00:20:05.771
30 plus years ago, I studied JFK,

00:20:05.771 --> 00:20:08.696
I studied Winston Churchill,
I also studied Hitler

00:20:08.696 --> 00:20:12.091
and his mannerisms, but I
couldn't understand what he said.

00:20:12.091 --> 00:20:16.148
And I studied to be a world
class speaker that I am today,

00:20:16.148 --> 00:20:18.815
or at least I'm told I am today.

00:20:20.423 --> 00:20:23.335
I studied Harry Truman who's up here

00:20:23.335 --> 00:20:25.040
who was the president that took over

00:20:25.040 --> 00:20:28.043
from Franklin Delano Roosevelt
when he died in office

00:20:28.043 --> 00:20:29.541
and he was the guy that made the decision

00:20:29.541 --> 00:20:31.869
to drop the atomic bomb, bombs.

00:20:31.869 --> 00:20:36.036
Can you just imagine the
heaviness of that decision?

00:20:36.952 --> 00:20:38.352
The heaviness that you're going to kill

00:20:38.352 --> 00:20:41.264
God knows how many people?

00:20:41.264 --> 00:20:43.847
I study, in current day I study

00:20:44.953 --> 00:20:48.685
Secretary of Defense General
Mattis, Mad Dog Mattis.

00:20:48.685 --> 00:20:51.552
And I have some friends
from my military days

00:20:51.552 --> 00:20:54.302
that actually know the secretary.

00:20:55.508 --> 00:20:57.606
But these are all high profile people.

00:20:57.606 --> 00:20:59.356
You may not like 'em,

00:21:00.230 --> 00:21:01.693
but they're high performance people,

00:21:01.693 --> 00:21:03.561
every single one of them.

00:21:03.561 --> 00:21:05.203
Every single one of them.

00:21:05.203 --> 00:21:09.470
And quite frankly, in
my judgment, 85 to 95%

00:21:09.470 --> 00:21:13.259
of the people that write
books aren't high performance.

00:21:13.259 --> 00:21:14.759
They're also rans.

00:21:16.313 --> 00:21:18.201
Why do the kids read 'em?

00:21:18.201 --> 00:21:19.059
Evan?

00:21:19.059 --> 00:21:21.309
Because they say it's easy.

00:21:23.361 --> 00:21:25.694
And I mean, high performance

00:21:26.716 --> 00:21:29.656
is anything but easy, and
staying on top is even harder

00:21:29.656 --> 00:21:31.856
than getting to the top.

00:21:31.856 --> 00:21:34.661
Now I've been on the top
of my game, arguably for

00:21:34.661 --> 00:21:37.434
three and a half decades.

00:21:37.434 --> 00:21:41.055
I haven't had to work in 35 years.

00:21:41.055 --> 00:21:44.982
People ask me how do I
get up in the morning?

00:21:44.982 --> 00:21:46.482
I get up fired up!

00:21:48.142 --> 00:21:52.520
I'm fired up, I've been
high on life since 1974,

00:21:52.520 --> 00:21:54.589
that I thought about it, and actually

00:21:54.589 --> 00:21:58.200
since I got that OCS 50 years ago today.

00:21:58.200 --> 00:22:00.278
Failure's not an option.

00:22:00.278 --> 00:22:01.950
And I do fail.

00:22:01.950 --> 00:22:05.239
But when I do fail I'm so fucking,

00:22:05.239 --> 00:22:06.883
I can't believe it!

00:22:06.883 --> 00:22:07.949
It must be an error!

00:22:07.949 --> 00:22:09.853
There must be a typo!

00:22:09.853 --> 00:22:13.252
Because I'm so used to winning.

00:22:13.252 --> 00:22:14.711
And I've had

00:22:14.711 --> 00:22:18.886
the pleasure, the good
fortune, to have been mentored

00:22:18.886 --> 00:22:20.469
by some real, real,

00:22:22.135 --> 00:22:25.016
world, world, world class guys.

00:22:25.016 --> 00:22:26.234
And,

00:22:26.234 --> 00:22:28.492
the world class guys like me.

00:22:28.492 --> 00:22:30.046
And,

00:22:30.046 --> 00:22:33.753
they often say you have the
energy I had 50, 60 years ago.

00:22:33.753 --> 00:22:36.003
This is when I was younger.

00:22:40.150 --> 00:22:41.483
I went where the action was.

00:22:41.483 --> 00:22:43.599
I went to New York.

00:22:43.599 --> 00:22:47.888
They said that Wall Street'd
eat me alive, barrio bad boy.

00:22:47.888 --> 00:22:49.221
They were wrong.

00:22:51.465 --> 00:22:54.473
I run towards the gunfire
and I kill everybody,

00:22:54.473 --> 00:22:56.905
metaphorically speaking.

00:22:56.905 --> 00:22:58.572
I look for problems.

00:22:59.843 --> 00:23:03.083
Because from chaos comes order.

00:23:03.083 --> 00:23:05.247
From chaos comes order, and I've done that

00:23:05.247 --> 00:23:07.497
successfully for, 50 years.

00:23:08.591 --> 00:23:12.604
And, I'll be 72 in a few
weeks, I don't feel 72,

00:23:12.604 --> 00:23:15.253
I don't believe I look 72.

00:23:15.253 --> 00:23:18.409
And I've had, if you've
noticed on my website,

00:23:18.409 --> 00:23:20.246
I'm called the bionic man because I've got

00:23:20.246 --> 00:23:24.011
so many artificial parts
in me, my knees, my hip,

00:23:24.011 --> 00:23:27.678
my shoulders, my
collarbone, my right bicep.

00:23:28.964 --> 00:23:32.688
I mean, I'm running out
of parts to replace.

00:23:32.688 --> 00:23:35.427
And that's because I do
everything to the maximum

00:23:35.427 --> 00:23:36.816
and I do a lot of physical stuff,

00:23:36.816 --> 00:23:40.983
in the past than now where I
got hurt a lot and I busted up.

00:23:45.799 --> 00:23:48.768
I'm looking to be all I
can be every single day.

00:23:48.768 --> 00:23:50.259
I mean, there's no question.

00:23:50.259 --> 00:23:52.212
And getting back to the original question,

00:23:52.212 --> 00:23:53.761
how do I change their mindset?

00:23:53.761 --> 00:23:56.565
Is because I require the
kids to be all they can be

00:23:56.565 --> 00:23:59.065
every single day for one year.

00:24:01.806 --> 00:24:05.885
I have 100% track record for
changing lives for the better.

00:24:05.885 --> 00:24:07.745
It's much less for billionaires.

00:24:07.745 --> 00:24:09.366
It's more for hundreds of millions

00:24:09.366 --> 00:24:11.711
and more even that than tens of millions,

00:24:11.711 --> 00:24:13.588
and if I can't make you the millionaire,

00:24:13.588 --> 00:24:16.255
I'll blow my fucking brains out.

00:24:17.641 --> 00:24:19.795
But I mean, a million, the
average little dumpy house

00:24:19.795 --> 00:24:23.212
in Los Angeles costs a million bucks now.

00:24:24.461 --> 00:24:27.524
I don't know about Canada but...

00:24:27.524 --> 00:24:29.441
- It's getting there,
Toronto's pretty expensive.

00:24:29.441 --> 00:24:32.072
- When I'm in Toronto, I'll probably stay

00:24:32.072 --> 00:24:33.760
at Trump Tower, which I stayed there

00:24:33.760 --> 00:24:36.596
last time I was in Toronto,
not because of President Trump.

00:24:36.596 --> 00:24:39.372
I don't know how close
that is to the University,

00:24:39.372 --> 00:24:40.455
I don't know.

00:24:42.525 --> 00:24:44.211
- Close enough.

00:24:44.211 --> 00:24:47.497
- I'm making two speeches in Toronto,

00:24:47.497 --> 00:24:50.330
one to a group of lawyers I think,

00:24:51.864 --> 00:24:54.372
financial, excuse me, financial people,

00:24:54.372 --> 00:24:56.539
and one to the university.

00:24:59.354 --> 00:25:01.854
And I'm looking forward to it,

00:25:03.511 --> 00:25:04.773
I'm expecting different kind of questions

00:25:04.773 --> 00:25:07.273
in Canada than I normally get.

00:25:08.118 --> 00:25:10.092
- I look at one guy on
the back of your wall,

00:25:10.092 --> 00:25:12.455
you got Ray Kroc who's the
guy who built McDonald's,

00:25:12.455 --> 00:25:15.327
and he really started that in his 60s.

00:25:15.327 --> 00:25:17.322
And at an age when most people
were thinking about retiring,

00:25:17.322 --> 00:25:18.966
that's when he's just getting started

00:25:18.966 --> 00:25:21.734
to go off and build this huge empire.

